{"term":"intentional","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a19886eff04f6c7522","definition":"Intended or planned; done deliberately or voluntarily.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":["deliberate"],"antonyms":["unintentional","undirected","accidental","unwitting"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["intentional community","intentional fallacy","intentional grounding","intentionalism","intentionalist","intentionalistic","intentionality","intentionally","intentional pass","intentional species","intentional walk","nonintentional","preterintentional"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intentional#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d3bcacc13334505428","definition":"Reflecting intention; marking an expenditure of will in the shape of a matter.","example":"It should, however, be borne in mind that even in the cohortative proper, the -ah does not add to the simple imperfect the ‘intentional’ signification expressed by that mood: the signification is already there, and the new termination merely renders it more prominent.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["purposeful","purposive","about","concerned with","oriented","advertent","conscious","witting","intentional","on purpose","volitational","volitional","voluntary","wilful"],"antonyms":["unintentional","undirected","accidental","unwitting"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["intentional community","intentional fallacy","intentional grounding","intentionalism","intentionalist","intentionalistic","intentionality","intentionally","intentional pass","intentional species","intentional walk","nonintentional","preterintentional"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intentional#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:57d3cfcc5ef1bdf1ac","definition":"Done with intent.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":["purposeful","purposive","about","concerned with","oriented","advertent","conscious","witting","intentional","on purpose","volitational","volitional","voluntary","wilful"],"antonyms":["unintentional","undirected","accidental","unwitting"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["intentional community","intentional fallacy","intentional grounding","intentionalism","intentionalist","intentionalistic","intentionality","intentionally","intentional pass","intentional species","intentional walk","nonintentional","preterintentional"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intentional#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ebca95b0369e8e0c0d","definition":"Object to intentionality, only appearing due to wilful perception.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":["purposeful","purposive","about","concerned with","oriented","advertent","conscious","witting","intentional","on purpose","volitational","volitional","voluntary","wilful"],"antonyms":["unintentional","undirected","accidental","unwitting"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["intentional community","intentional fallacy","intentional grounding","intentionalism","intentionalist","intentionalistic","intentionality","intentionally","intentional pass","intentional species","intentional walk","nonintentional","preterintentional"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intentional#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:012c25e170e302aa39","definition":"Directed toward or about a foci of attentional consciousness; possessing the property of being a consciousness of something.","example":"It is of the very nature of consciousness to be intentional and a consciousness that would cease to be consciousness of something would for that very reason cease to exist.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["purposeful","purposive","about","concerned with","oriented","advertent","conscious","witting","intentional","on purpose","volitational","volitional","voluntary","wilful"],"antonyms":["unintentional","undirected","accidental","unwitting"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["intentional community","intentional fallacy","intentional grounding","intentionalism","intentionalist","intentionalistic","intentionality","intentionally","intentional pass","intentional species","intentional walk","nonintentional","preterintentional"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intentional#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6f815d90f051ec473f","definition":"Something that has no essential underlying structure but apparition only as defined by perception; object only because consciousness is directed to it.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":["intentional community","intentional fallacy","intentional grounding","intentionalism","intentionalist","intentionalistic","intentionality","intentionally","intentional pass","intentional species","intentional walk","nonintentional","preterintentional"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intentional#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:059586405a5bbf6f43","definition":"The cohortative mood as found in Hebrew (terminology borrowed from Julius Friedrich Böttcher † 1863 and now outmoded), and constructions of similar purpose in even more exotic languages.","example":"Tariana distinguishes interrogative and imperative moods. Interrogative mood is marked through a separate set of evidentials fused with tense (see §14.2). Imperatives are discussed in §16.1. Modalities include: frustrative (§16.2), intentional (§16.3), apprehensive (§16.4), uncertainty (§16.5), conditional (§16.6), purposive (§16.7) and counter-expectation (§16.8). […] The intentional is marked with the clitic -kasu. It can occur with any group of verbs, marking imminent action, as in 16.60 and intention, as in 16.61.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["intentional community","intentional fallacy","intentional grounding","intentionalism","intentionalist","intentionalistic","intentionality","intentionally","intentional pass","intentional species","intentional walk","nonintentional","preterintentional"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intentional#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ɪnˈtɛnʃn̩(ə)l/"},"wordFamily":["intentional community","intentional fallacy","intentional grounding","intentionalism","intentionalist","intentionalistic","intentionality","intentionally","intentional pass","intentional species","intentional walk","nonintentional","preterintentional"]}